Provision with services.postgresql: enable the server, list database names in
ensureDatabases, and create users via ensureUsers. Grant a user ownership of a
database by setting that user's ensureDBOwnership to true -- nixpkgs grants
ownership of the database whose name matches the user's name, so the database
and the owning user must share a name. Do not set passwords and do not write
SQL by hand. Reference database and user names as string values.

ensureUsers is a list of attrsets: emit it as
services.postgresql.ensureUsers with a rhs value of
[ { name = "<user>"; ensureDBOwnership = true; } ] -- a list whose one element
is an attrset with a name field (the program value) and an ensureDBOwnership
field (the literal true). The kernel's value grammar supports attrsets.
